& -1 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]$ has the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{33}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069826/state.json" "file_sha256" "b73e7e81e0fea47c1a6e62b729081f627ce063945538b6e791b9bfcb4bfd55f2"} {"question" "q-106858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{2}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot {E}_{1}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{3}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot {E}_{2}\\cdot {E}_{1}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{3},$ ${E}_{2},$ and ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ {E}_{2}{E}_{1}A & ={E}_{3}^{-1}U \\\\ {E}_{1}A & ={E}_{2}^{-1}{E}_{3}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}^{-1}{E}_{3}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & =([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}])U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-1,$ ${u}_{33}=4,$ and ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{33}=-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069826/state.json" "file_sha256" "b73e7e81e0fea47c1a6e62b729081f627ce063945538b6e791b9bfcb4bfd55f2"} {"question" "q-106858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069826/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e1f1c1e81892c4d56976feff83c2f8efe47113a042e3674b1229c69cfdee3f1"} {"question" "q-106858" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069826/state.json" "file_sha256" "b73e7e81e0fea47c1a6e62b729081f627ce063945538b6e791b9bfcb4bfd55f2"} {"question" "q-106858" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "-6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069826/state.json" "file_sha256" "b73e7e81e0fea47c1a6e62b729081f627ce063945538b6e791b9bfcb4bfd55f2"} {"question" "q-106858" "field" "selection" "a